course: dictionary
lesson: 13156
title: Forgotten: not remembered
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To forget something means you cannot bring it back into your mind. Its past form is forgot, and the past participle is forgotten, which you use with have or has: «I have forgotten my password.» Here forgotten means you did not keep the password in your mind.
explain: Forgotten can also describe a noun, so it works as an adjective. «We found a forgotten toy under the bed.» The toy is not lost in a box; nobody remembers it or plays with it any more. Look at the clues: have forgotten tells you about an action, and a forgotten toy tells you about the toy.
explain: The words around forgotten give clues. «Long forgotten» means nobody has remembered it for a long time. «Forgive and forget» means let go of anger and stop thinking about the hurt. Ask yourself: is someone failing to remember, or has something stopped being cared about?
explain: At school, a forgotten PE kit is one you left at home. In a story, a forgotten village may be found again by explorers. If you see a bag that someone has forgotten at a station or airport, do not touch it. Tell a member of staff straight away.
fact: «Forgotten» is the past participle of «forget»: forget, forgot, forgotten.
fact: As an adjective, «forgotten» means no longer remembered or cared about by people.
fact: Use «have forgotten» or «has forgotten» with another verb: «She has forgotten her homework.»
fact: «Long forgotten» means that nobody has remembered it for a long time.
fact: Never touch a forgotten bag; tell staff so they can check it safely.
exercise: «I have ___ my PE kit.» Which form of forget fits the gap? | *forgotten | forgot | forget | forgetting
exercise: «The forgotten village was found by explorers.» What does forgotten mean here? | Very angry | Left behind on a train | *No longer remembered by people | Found by a dog
exercise: Which phrase means let go of a hurt and stop remembering it? | *Forgive and forget | Forgotten homework | Forgetting the time | Long forgotten
test: «The team has ___ their lunch boxes.» Pick the right word for the gap. | forget | forgets | forgot | *forgotten
test: You see a bag that someone has forgotten at the station. What should you do? | Take it home to keep it safe | Kick it out of the way | Open it to find the owner | *Do not touch it; tell a member of staff
exam: Which sentence uses forgotten as an adjective? | She forgot to lock the door. | *We walked past a forgotten church in the woods. | I have forgotten my book. | He forgets his name sometimes.
